## Context

User identified <https://github.com/ruvnet/ruflo> as a high-value reference project:

- ~60 production agents in an Enterprise AI Orchestration Platform
- 22.4k GitHub stars
- User believes we can learn a lot and potentially reuse agents or flows directly rather than re-implementing them

## Goal

Decide whether OwlBear should directly adopt, selectively adapt, or only reference ruflo's agent and orchestration patterns, then turn that recommendation into concrete follow-up tasks if warranted.

## Scope

- Research only. Do not import Ruflo packages, copy its agent files wholesale, or modify OwlBear source code as part of this task.
- Analyze Ruflo repository contents via local clone when possible; if cloning is not possible in the current environment, use raw repository files and directory views and record that limitation in the research doc.
- Compare Ruflo patterns against OwlBear's existing agent, hook, prompt-context, daemon, and notification seams rather than evaluating them in isolation.
- If the recommendation implies engineering work, create ideation tasks that link back to the research doc. Do not implicitly approve those implementation tasks as part of this research card.

## OwlBear Integration Seams

- .github/agents/*.agent.md
- src/owlbear/core/hooks.py
- src/owlbear/bootstrap/hooks.py
- src/owlbear/core/agent.py
- src/owlbear/core/board_context.py
- src/owlbear/memory/context.py
- src/owlbear/core/notification_hook.py
- src/owlbear/daemon.py
- src/owlbear/bootstrap/channel.py

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Create docs/research/ruflo-analysis.md with sections for context/question, sources studied, architecture-fit comparison, agent-overlap map, adoption-mode comparison, recommendation, and follow-up tasks.
- [ ] Document Ruflo's agent taxonomy, orchestration model, tool/plugin patterns, and LLM/runtime wiring from repository sources; if local cloning is unavailable, explicitly record the fallback access method used.
- [ ] Map the relevant Ruflo agent roles to OwlBear analogs in .github/agents/*.agent.md and state a reuse verdict for each mapped role: direct adoption, selective adaptation, or inspiration-only.
- [ ] Evaluate licensing compatibility from Ruflo's published license and state both what OwlBear is legally allowed to copy/reference and what it should operationally avoid.
- [ ] Identify 3-5 highest-value patterns or agent capabilities to adopt first and tie each to a concrete OwlBear integration seam listed above.
- [ ] Compare direct adoption, selective adaptation, and inspiration-only reference, and end with exactly one recommendation.
- [ ] If the recommendation implies engineering work, execute kanban-md create commands for each follow-up task at ideation status and ensure each new task points back to docs/research/ruflo-analysis.md; otherwise explicitly state why no follow-up tasks were created.
- [ ] Update docs/sources/overview.md for the external Ruflo materials used in the research.

## Research

- Local clone attempt in `docs/scratch/research/ruflo` failed in this environment, so the analysis used raw repo files and GitHub directory pages from the live repository.
- Verdict: adaptation only. Do not import Ruflo packages or copy its agent files directly; reuse the patterns instead.
- Best-fit patterns: hook-triggered background workers, config-driven reaction routing, runtime prompt assembly, and priority-routed notifications.
- Follow-up tasks created: #949 background worker pilot, #950 HookEvent reaction routing, #951 runtime prompt context injection, #952 priority-routed notifications.
- Created commands:
  - `kanban\kanban-md.exe create "Design hook-triggered background worker pilot for audit map testgaps and document flows" ...` -> #949
  - `kanban\kanban-md.exe create "Implement config-driven HookEvent reaction routing with retry and escalation" ...` -> #950
  - `kanban\kanban-md.exe create "Inject runtime task and workspace context into dispatched agent prompts" ...` -> #951
  - `kanban\kanban-md.exe create "Add priority-routed notifications for daemon and pipeline events" ...` -> #952
- Attribution updated in `docs/sources/overview.md`.
- Research doc: `docs/research/ruflo-analysis.md`